<title>GREECE: GREEK M3 RISE PROVISIONALLY 15.5PCT Y/Y IN MAY.</title>
<headline>GREEK M3 RISE PROVISIONALLY 15.5PCT Y/Y IN MAY.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greek M3 money supply grew</p>
<p>provisionally 15.5 percent year-on-year in May from a revised</p>
<p>14.4 percent in April, overshooting the central bank's 6.0-9.0</p>
<p>percent target range at end-97, the Bank of Greece said in a</p>
<p>statement.</p>
<p>The acceleration of M3 was due to the continuing portfolio</p>
<p>reshuffling by private investors away from T-bills towards</p>
<p>deposits, it added.</p>
<p>M4 money supply grew provisionally 8.6 percent year-on-year</p>
<p>in May from a revised 9.1 percent in April, it said.</p>
<p>    M3 money supply	     May 97     April 97     May 96</p>
<p>    Stock (bln drachmas)     19,082.6    19,194.4     16,525.7</p>
<p>    Yr-on-yr (pct)		15.5	   14.4	   9.3</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
